## Selected direction and exact scope

The user selected Orris Liquid as the richest remembered orris-root material and rejected Irotyl for smell and texture. Their later direct stock correction was **9% w/w in DEP**. Both facts were recovered from the source task and verified against the saved selected-direction brief and dated stock overlay. The source task also records that the fragrance is still being planned.

V4 preserves every non-iris V3 dose. It replaces the entire 1,050 µL iris basket with Orris Liquid, reduced Alpha Isomethyl Ionone, reduced Alpha Ionone, and reduced Alpha Irone. Irotyl, Dihydro Beta Ionone, Ultralia, Orivone, and Carrot Seed EO are omitted. The latter four are not certified absent from Dior; they are removed to give the preferred Orris product a clearer, independently testable role. Irotyl is explicitly excluded by the user's target and sensory preference.

**Bottle target:** 30 mL nominal. **Raw-stock concentrate:** 6,000 µL. **Diluent:** 24,000 µL Ethanol 96%. **Nominal sum:** 30,000 µL, at 20% v/v raw-stock concentrate under additive-volume convention. This is not 20% neat odorants or 20% w/w. Mixing contraction and delivery loss are not measured. Use a vessel with sufficient headroom; do not force the blend into an exactly brim-full container.

## Research: ingredient identity and evidence

1. Dior's house description supports Tuscan iris, ambrette-related fruity talc, Virginia cedar, amber and woods. Its current international disclosure shows code 10950/A, not 05443/A. Current-page alpha-isomethyl ionone and coumarin disclosure is not a verified 2011 ingredient list. [Dior product](https://www.dior.com/en_int/beauty/products/dior-homme-intense-Y0479201.html)
2. Dior's own Ukrainian page identifies the 2011 creation with François Demachy. That corroborates lineage; it does not disclose the archived concentrate. [Dior historical copy](https://www.dior.com/uk_ua/beauty/products/dior-homme-intense-Y0479201.html)
3. The named 2011 lavender/iris/ambrette/pear/cedar/vetiver sequence in the parent derives partly from contemporaneous secondary reporting. Treat it as reference architecture, not an analytical peak list. No authenticated 05443/A chromatogram with standards and quantified uncertainty was available for this revision.
4. PerfumersWorld Orris Liquid, SKU 8IQ24653, is the user's selected supplied product. The supplier describes powdery floral wood, cosmetic violet, root-associated facets, and a creamy drydown. This supports a candidate role; it does not prove the exact product is in Dior. The supplier's irone-range description is not this stock's lot assay. Its product density must not be applied to the prepared 9% DEP stock. [Orris Liquid](https://www.perfumersworld.com/view.php?pro_id=8IQ24653)
5. Alpha Ionone, Alpha Isomethyl Ionone and Alpha Irone are separate identities. The selected methyl-ionone bottle is the inventory row “Alpha Isomethyl Ionone (Methyl Ionone Pure)”; a different Givaudan AIMI grade or Methyl Ionone Gamma Coeur is not silently interchangeable. [Supplier methyl ionone](https://www.perfumersworld.com/view.php?pro_id=3IW00300)
6. Primary work on separated irone isomers demonstrates why a whole orris product cannot be reduced to a generic alpha-irone label or assumed sensory equivalent from total irone content. [Brenna, Fuganti and Serra, 2003](https://comptes-rendus.academie-sciences.fr/chimie/articles/en/10.1016/S1631-0748(03)00087-0/)
7. The supplier's linked Alpha Irone COA has a generic compound description and no lot-matched purity/isomer assay. It cannot certify the user's stock as stereochemically pure alpha-irone. Preserve stock identity while withholding that stronger claim. [Supplier COA](https://www.perfumersworld.com/ifra/COA/8II00243.pdf)

The generic local iris guide's Irotyl recommendation and older reverse-engineering assertions of exact Dior proportions are not admissible ingredient evidence. The four iris ingredients here are design choices mapped to identified stocks. Their inclusion is not a claim that all four occur in DHI2011.

## TARGET / IDEAL architecture

| Target function | Ideal evidence-led material specification | Current build mapping | Unresolved gap |
|---|---|---|---|
| Rich orris root as the named heart | Reference-fit, lot-qualified orris product with documented composition and sensory comparison | User's preferred Orris Liquid, 9% w/w DEP | No authenticated Dior material/lot match; no measured headspace or purity |
| Supporting cosmetic powder | Identified methyl-ionone grade chosen against reference | Alpha Isomethyl Ionone inventory bottle | Grade and stereochemistry are not disclosed Dior facts |
| Violet movement | Only as much woody-violet contour as root needs | Reduced Alpha Ionone | Omission/alternative comparison outstanding |
| Root accent | Independently adjustable iris accent if it improves the supplied orris product | Reduced Alpha Irone 10% w/w DEP | Pure-irone assay and extra-accent need unverified |
| Lavender-to-fruity ambrette/talc | Fine lavender, a small fruit glint, reference-fit ambrette material | Inherited V3 lavender, fruit, Ambrettolide and powder supports | Ambrettolide is a proxy, not ambrette seed; literal pear chemicals unknown |
| Warm cedar/vetiver landing | Dry Virginia cedar, restrained vetiver and coumarinic/vanillic warmth | Fixed V3 frame | Full recipe similarity and smoothness NOT TESTED |

These are target functions, not a purported ideal Dior ingredient list or invented proprietary percentages. Irotyl has no slot. Complexity is the richness and temporal relationship of these functions, not the number of rows.

## CURRENT-INVENTORY BUILD

**Exact-mass rule:** for a stock with known mass fraction f and measured delivered stock mass m_i, product mass is f × m_i and concentrate ppm w/w is 1,000,000 × f × m_i / total delivered concentrate mass. Pure-material assay, where unknown, is separate from supplied-product mass. For neat/as-supplied stocks, delivered volume is known by the card but certified pure chemical mass is not assumed. For Mimosa, Osmanthus and E2MB the recorded percent basis remains unspecified; exact active mass is HOLD even if delivered stock mass is measured.

The “model proxy” below is raw volume × nominal fraction, supplied solely to reconcile the existing simulator. It is not literal active volume for w/w stocks. Exact ppm w/w is HOLD for the complete formula because the measured mass chain is absent. No density is invented. The pipeline's own density assumptions and composite OAV are disclosed in its output and remain screening estimates.

