## Retained-material decisions

Each role below is a testable hypothesis, not observed success. Retaining the non-iris frame makes this an interpretable module revision, but does not prove every inherited helper earns its place.

| Material | Distinct target-linked function and omission test |
|---|---|
| Hedione | Floral air at the iris edge; omission tests opacity. Held at V3 dose, not enlarged for score. |
| Iso E Super | Transparent cedar transition; distinct from literal Virginia cedar. Omission tests abrupt wood entry; generic wood takeover is failure. |
| Benzyl Salicylate | Cosmetic film hypothesis; distinct from neutral benzoate mass. Below-threshold status cannot prove this effect. |
| Benzyl Benzoate | Low-odor replacement space and solvent-like mass; no recognizable note claimed. |
| Vetiver EO (India) | Owned Indian Vetiver EO volume grade; earthy counterline to powder, distinct from cedar and smoother Vetival. |
| Cedarwood oil Virginia | Named cedar facet of house architecture; distinct from abstract Iso E. Omission tests late wood recognition. |
| Cashmeran | Warm textile link between powder and wood; neither a musk replacement nor evidence of literal cashmere. |
| Sandalore | Inherited cedar-to-musk rounding hypothesis. No sandalwood lead; first non-iris omission candidate if no repeatable loss. |
| Vetival | Polished dry woody-vetiver transition; less earthy than natural vetiver. Compare its omission against retained natural vetiver. |
| Ambrettolide | Fruity skin-musk proxy for ambrette relation. Not ambrette seed oil or proof of the Dior musk. |
| Ethylene Brassylate | Creamy textile body behind iris; distinct from Ambrettolide fruit and Romandolide outward wood. Musk blanket is failure. |
| Romandolide | Outward woody-musk extension; distinct hypothesis from inward fruity Ambrettolide and EB body. |
| Lavender EO High Altitude | Fine aromatic entry from owned French stock; selected over spike/camphor lavender. Must yield to iris. |
| Linalyl Acetate | Soft ester transition from lavender into fruit; distinct from linalool floral freshness. |
| Linalool | Small floral continuation of lavender, held fixed; omission tests the aromatic-to-floral edge. |
| Mimosa Absolute | Inherited powder irregularity; not a claimed Dior ingredient. Yellow-flower naming or no omission loss disqualifies it. |
| Osmanthus Absolute | Inherited fruit-to-violet transition hypothesis; premium 10% stock, not volume grade. Apricot takeover disqualifies it. |
| Orris Liquid | User-selected rich root lead, PW 8IQ24653 product. Distinct whole-product character; no pure-irone assay assumed. |
| Alpha Isomethyl Ionone (Methyl Ionone Pure) | Reduced cosmetic powder support around Orris Liquid; do not substitute unresolved Givaudan AIMI grade. |
| Alpha Ionone | Reduced woody-violet motion connecting fruit and root; separate molecule and role from methyl ionone. |
| Alpha Irone | Reduced independently adjustable iris accent. Tests whether the added Orris product can carry the root identity. |
| Tonkarome | Inherited coumarinic warmth; not pure coumarin and not a certified Dior ingredient. |
| Isobutavan | Separate soft vanillic transition into musk. Cream or dessert recognition before iris is failure. |
| Verdox | Inherited green fruit body leading into woods; pear is an accord hypothesis, not a chemical identity. |
| Benzyl Acetate | Inherited floral-fruit bridge, distinct from Verdox wood/green. Banana or jasmine takeover is failure. |
| Ethyl 2-Methylbutyrate | Prepared dilute fruit flash; separate volatile role from Verdox. Carrier recorded in canonical parent binding, basis unspecified. |

## Full inventory review and nonredundancy

| Live inventory category reviewed | Decision for this revision |
|---|---|
| Solvents/carriers | Keep V3 ethanol addition; inherited DPG/TEC and confirmed Orris/Irone DEP stay in raw doses. Do not add IPM, extra DPG or an unmeasured water adjustment. |
| Citrus/top | Keep linalool, linalyl acetate and diluted E2MB already in the parent. Citrus oils, aldehydes and additional fruit esters would change the opening comparison. |
| Green/fresh/marine | Keep only inherited Verdox. Exclude aquatic, ozone, mint, eucalyptus, galbanic and aggressive leaf materials; no target-linked gap supports them. |
| Floral materials | Keep inherited Hedione, salicylate/benzoate, benzyl acetate, mimosa, osmanthus and Isobutavan. No rose, muguet or narcotic-floral additions; the root must remain identifiable. |
| Iris/violet | Selected four rows replace the old eight. Beta Ionone, Allyl Ionone, violet leaf, Irotyl and extra grades are not default iris fillers. No new carrot/Orivone increase. |
| Woods/amber/structure | Keep V3 cedar, vetiver, Vetival, Iso E, Cashmeran and Sandalore. Owned Bacdanol and Benzyl Salicylate status is recognized; Bacdanol's new sandalwood mass is unnecessary here. |
| Musks | Keep the three V3 doses for the module comparison; do not stack Habanolide, Zenolide, Galaxolide or Exaltolide. Depleted exception-only musks remain excluded. |
| Sweet/gourmand/balsamic | Keep Tonkarome and Isobutavan. Coumarin 20% DEP is owned in the c4d5 authority; its unspecified fraction basis is HOLD, not unavailability. Literal cocoa/coffee, maltol, extra tonka/resins would obscure the selected root question. |
| Leather/smoke/phenolics | None added. No evidence requires a leather, smoke, oud or moss recognizer for this selected direction. |
| Spice/aromatic | Keep selected lavender. No pepper, saffron, clove, incense, cypress or patchouli addition is justified by this revision. |
| Accord bases/other | No opaque bases or corrective accords added. |

**Musk pairwise distinctions:** Ambrettolide versus EB tests fruity skin mediation versus creamy powder body; Ambrettolide versus Romandolide tests inward fruit continuity versus outward woody extension; EB versus Romandolide tests body versus projection. These are hypotheses, not completed nonredundancy demonstrations. Controlled omission of each must preserve the other two and match the omitted stock carrier. If no repeatable distinct loss appears, the redundant musk should be removed in a later version. No present evidence establishes a universal winning chord.

The same caution applies to Benzyl Salicylate versus Benzyl Benzoate (cosmetic-film hypothesis versus structural reservoir), and Sandalore versus Cashmeran (rounding hypothesis versus textile warmth). Below-threshold helpers earn no note credit.

## Parent delta and carrier accounting

The non-iris subtotal is 4,950 µL and remains identical to V3. The iris subtotal remains 1,050 µL:

| Iris material | V3 raw | V4 raw | Intended change |
|---|---:|---:|---|
| Orris Liquid 9% w/w DEP | 0 | 510 | New root-richness source selected by the user |
| Alpha Isomethyl Ionone | 420 | 300 | Reduce powder competition |
| Alpha Ionone | 180 | 120 | Reduce independent violet competition |
| Alpha Irone 10% w/w DEP | 180 | 120 | Reduce isolated accent when whole Orris product enters |
| Dihydro Beta Ionone | 100 | 0 | Remove unproved late-iris helper |
| Irotyl | 80 | 0 | Explicit user exclusion |
| Ultralia | 60 | 0 | Remove unproved recurrence helper |
| Orivone | 20 | 0 | Do not add a second root contour before testing preferred product |
| Carrot Seed EO | 10 | 0 | Omit botanical accent for the first comparison |

No stock-strength rebase is performed. These are deliberate dose/composition changes. A constant raw total does not mean constant active amount or constant carrier composition. Mixed-basis simulator proxy changes from V3 4,010.05 to V4 3,599.95 µL-equivalent. It is NOT a physical active-volume measurement.

For measured delivered masses:
- Orris stock: product = 0.09 m_O; DEP = 0.91 m_O.
- Alpha Irone stock: supplied-product equivalent = 0.10 m_I; DEP = 0.90 m_I.
- Ambrettolide stock: supplied product = 0.10 m_A; DPG = 0.90 m_A.
- Tonkarome stock: supplied base = 0.20 m_T; TEC = 0.80 m_T.
- Mimosa, Osmanthus and E2MB: carrier is named DPG; its exact mass/volume split remains HOLD until fraction basis is established.

For illustration ONLY under a hypothetical stock density of 1.000 g/mL, the 510 µL Orris transfer would contain 45.9 mg supplied product and 464.1 mg DEP, while the 120 µL Alpha Irone transfer would contain 12 mg supplied product and 108 mg DEP. That density is not measured or adopted as physical truth; do not print these proxy masses on a production label. The Orris product is not 9% pure irones.

The raw×fraction carrier proxy is DEP 572.1, DPG 1,579.95, TEC 248.0 µL-equivalent, total 2,400.05. The DEP proxy rises by 410.1 against V3. Exact carrier displacement and exact active ppm are HOLD. The V3-versus-V4 sensory contrast therefore includes vehicle change and cannot isolate molecular causes.

