## Verification provenance and claim limits

This artifact is written in isolated c4d5 at baseline 0af42cc68730499f54b7c29c67c2320a3f92a9a2. The immediate V3 parent and the newer Orris DEP correction were read from D:/chatbots/perfume-chem; the parent hash above freezes exactly what was compared. The checkouts differ in inventory authority. Canonical records do not erase c4d5's newer Coumarin DEP ownership or reinstate unavailable Ambrofix. No engine, tests, governance or inventory files were edited.

The current c4d5 Orris label is stale about carrier; its YAML additionally has a stale 30% stock and an alpha-irone-equivalent composite. Existing model values must be labeled as such. All natural mixtures (lavender, cedar, vetiver, mimosa, osmanthus and Orris Liquid) must use the existing composite path, with coverage checked. Orris's 82.5% modeled irone pool is a literature/supplier-derived approximation, not a lot assay. Exact ODT and OAV for the actual bottle are unknown.

Functionally required rows below OAV 1 must be flagged; no formula dose will be raised simply to cross a modeled threshold. IFRA/allergen results, including missing limits and natural constituent uncertainty, remain limitations. This developmental composition is not certified safe, stable, similar to Dior, liked, or commercially released.

