### Parent acceptance and unresolved boundaries

**Outcome: DEVELOPMENT RECIPE COMPLETE; STOCK-BINDING, EXACT-MASS, SAFETY AND SENSORY HOLD.**

The final diagnostic returned 109 PASS / 34 WARN / 2 FAIL (plus one SKIP). Both failures trace to stock/preflight authority. G15 dose-lineage plus OAV-per-time screening passed with the immediate V3 parent supplied. The architecture-only reference contract passed; neither pass proves that the formula contains Dior's actual ingredient set or smells like DHI2011.

| Unresolved stock binding | Verified interpretation | Required next action |
|---|---|---|
| Alpha Isomethyl Ionone (Methyl Ionone Pure) | c4d5 reports two live stock variants; its runtime normalization may select a different Givaudan AIMI identity | Reconcile the selected physical bottle and unique stock ID through the governed stock authority. No silent grade substitution. |
| Ambrettolide | c4d5 requirements still report preparation_required despite the newer canonical 10% w/w DPG preparation correction | Integrate that existing preparation evidence through the normal authority workflow; do not ask the user to repeat the correction. |
| Tonkarome | Owned, but c4d5 stock metadata is incomplete; canonical records specify the homogeneous 20% w/w TEC preparation | Integrate the existing preparation evidence, preserving basis and carrier. |
| Vetiver EO (India) | V3 parser name is not bound by c4d5 to the physically listed Indian Vetiver EO volume-grade stock | Reconcile the exact existing stock/alias; this is not evidence that the user has no vetiver. |

The newer Orris correction is already known: 9% w/w supplied product in DEP, record INV-USER-20260905-001. It was honored in this formula. c4d5's older carrier entry must not reverse the user's correction. Canonical and c4d5 authority bundles both materialize successfully; this run is NOT an overlay-hash-drift failure. Do not wholesale copy canonical inventory: its other entries conflict with newer c4d5 ownership/stock corrections. No governance pins were changed.

The first run's reference failure was a negation-insensitive text scan in engine/reference_contracts.py: the tokens "quantitative" and "ratios" triggered stronger claim detection even in disclaimers. Formula-only wording was clarified, preserving the architecture-only scope and all mass/assay limits; the second run passed that reference check. No detector code or gate thresholds were changed. Exact ppm w/w remains unavailable and is a WARN for this held diagnostic, not suddenly available after the wording edit.

The scanner's "27 material(s) with unspecified concentration basis" message does not match the primary parsed recipe: there are 26 rows, with explicit neat/mass-fraction declarations except Mimosa Absolute, Osmanthus Absolute and Ethyl 2-Methylbutyrate. Those three genuine basis gaps remain HOLD. The scanner message is preserved, not accepted as 27 independent missing preparations. Measured delivered masses and appropriate mixture-basis documentation are still needed for an exact complete ppm w/w chain. A density fallback is not a measurement.

**Perfumer judgment:** "Orris-led" is the selected design direction, not an achieved perceptual result. The Orris product is the largest raw transfer within the iris basket because it is only 9% stock. Its modeled opening OAV is 5.660, versus Alpha Ionone 92.878, the methyl-ionone proxy 39.266, and Alpha Irone 1.383. At 4 h those values are 5.543, 87.848, 38.564 and 1.356 respectively. This does not certify root dominance or authorize increasing Orris to chase a numerical score. The required result is recognition and preference in the complete, controlled blend.

Iso E Super, lavender and Hedione lead the modeled opening signal. The model assigns some familiar opening materials to heart, and all 26 gamma values have predictive/heuristic/fallback/unknown authority; the summed OAV family chart cannot establish perceived composition. The 18% iris-family floor is an advisory stored rule, not evidence for Dior's proprietary loading. No material was added to satisfy an arbitrary score or ingredient-count target.

Sandalore (opening OAV 0.1503) and Benzyl Salicylate (0.0430) earn no demonstrated perceptible rounding/cosmetic credit. They remain inherited, explicitly unproved omission candidates. Benzyl Benzoate (0.00140) has only a structural role. Ethyl 2-Methylbutyrate falls to OAV 0.975 at 4 h; its intended opening role does not require drydown perceptibility. No missing late fruit is inferred. All other non-structural rows remain above modeled OAV 1 in the five sampled windows, which is not proof that they are recognizable in mixture.

The generic receptor-saturation caps, cedrol sedation association, Tonkarome glycoside mechanism, Alpha Irone captive/pricing statement, fixed aesthetic heuristics, and zero-valued authority scores in the formatter are not independently validated conclusions for these physical stocks. The "12.0% active" line is a mixed-basis volume proxy, not exact finished-product mass concentration. The uncalibrated 3.8% loss index is not measured evaporation, skin life or stability. Missing IFRA limits and constituent uncertainty mean no skin-use or sale clearance was obtained.

**Next authorized formulation step:** preserve this complete candidate and resolve the stock bindings and three fraction-basis gaps before issuing a ready-to-mix card. Subsequent blind V3/V4 and carrier-matched Orris-omission comparisons are specified above. Inventory/engine synchronization is a separate scope; it was not performed here.

